WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.600
Volcanic inclusions can bring pieces of older rocks toward the surface.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.560
Uplift and erosion can expose rocks that once formed at depth.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.480
Mines expose rocks along excavated workings.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.880
Drill cores recover cylindrical samples along boreholes.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.100
These are direct observations with limited spatial coverage, not a complete

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.740
view of Earth’s interior. Surface outcrops and mine material can offer

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.140
accessible evidence of subsurface rock types.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.520
Check where a sample came from before using it to reconstruct

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.460
its original position.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:35.600
Seismic-reflection surveys send energy into the ground and record returning signals

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:41.100
with geophones. Reflections can reveal boundaries, folds, faults, and layered geometry.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.800
Magnetic surveys measure variations in magnetic field strength related to rock

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:51.560
properties. Gravity surveys measure small gravitational variations related to density contrasts.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.740
Electrical surveys measure conductivity or resistivity.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:58.780
Water-bearing material and clay can influence electrical response;

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.520
a conductive anomaly does not uniquely identify one rock type.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:08.900
The buried-channel example combines low-density sediment, relatively low magnetism, and a

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.420
conductivity pattern consistent with wetter material.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.080
Each measurement constrains a different property.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.500
A seismic profile is processed data;

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.360
a colored geologic cross section is an interpretation based on those

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.300
data and other evidence. They are not the same kind of

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:27.720
observation. Several subsurface configurations may fit one data set.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.520
Combining samples, geology, and multiple surveys helps reduce ambiguity.
